---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
import { getSitePage, REVIEWED_DATE, REVIEWED_ISO } from "../data/sitePages";

const page = getSitePage("/privacy/");
const c = site.company;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={page.title}
  description={page.description}
  alternateMd="/privacy/index.md"
  pageType="WebPage"
  dateModified={REVIEWED_ISO}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Privacy" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="small">Last reviewed: {REVIEWED_DATE}</p>
      <p class="lead" style="font-size:1.05rem;color:var(--ink-2)">
        This policy explains what personal data we receive for a quotation or order, where it is processed, how long
        it is kept and how to exercise your rights. It also states what this website does not collect.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who controls your data</h2>
      <p>
        {site.brand} is a trading name of {c.legalNameEn}, an individual business registered in {c.city},
        {c.region}, {c.country} under USCC {c.uscc}. That legal entity is the controller. Privacy contact:
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Privacy`}>{site.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. The honest limits of this site</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static site with no account, cart, login, analytics, advertising tag, social embed, heatmap or A/B
        testing script. Personal data reaches us only when you send an enquiry, provide artwork or place an order. The
        only browser storage we know of is the necessary Cloudflare security cookie on the <a href="/cookies/">cookies
        page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Data we collect</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Examples</th><th scope="col">When collected</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Legal basis (GDPR)</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Enquiry and quotation</td><td>Name, company, email, phone or WhatsApp, destination and specification</td><td>When you ask for a quote</td><td>To answer and prepare the quotation</td><td>Steps before a contract; legitimate interests in correspondence</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Order and delivery</td><td>Billing and delivery address, quantity, price, shipping reference and carrier updates</td><td>When an order is confirmed</td><td>To produce, invoice and ship it</td><td>Contract; legal obligation for records</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Artwork and proofs</td><td>Design files, fonts, images, dielines, approvals and technical notes</td><td>When you send artwork</td><td>To check and print the order</td><td>Contract or pre-contract steps; consent where a file identifies a person</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Payment records</td><td>Invoice reference, amount, currency, transfer date and remittance confirmation; no card data through this site</td><td>When payment is made</td><td>To receive payment and meet accounting duties</td><td>Contract; legal obligation; legitimate interests in fraud prevention</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Security logs</td><td>IP address, requested URL, user agent, timestamp and challenge result</td><td>Automatically with a request</td><td>To serve the site and detect abuse</td><td>Legitimate interests in security; legal obligation where required</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>4. What we do not collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Payment-card numbers, security codes or online-banking passwords through this website.</li>
        <li>Government identity documents or tax identifiers unless an invoice field requires one and you choose to send it.</li>
        <li>Date of birth, family or health information.</li>
        <li>Precise location, location history or a behavioural advertising profile.</li>
        <li>Account credentials, saved baskets or quote history, because none exist.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Legal bases and consent</h2>
      <p>
        We rely on contract or pre-contract steps, legal obligations for accounting records, and legitimate interests
        in correspondence, security and fraud prevention. Consent is used only for a genuinely optional permission,
        such as publishing a photograph or case study. You can withdraw consent at any time without affecting earlier
        processing.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Processors and other recipients</h2>
      <p>
        We share only what is needed. Cloudflare is named because it is the confirmed hosting and CDN provider; for
        other providers we give the category and can confirm the current name in a processing agreement.
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Recipient</th><th scope="col">Role</th><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Location</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Hosting, CDN and bot management</td><td>Request metadata, IP and security cookie data</td><td>Global network</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email provider</td><td>Business email and file transfer</td><td>Enquiry, order and artwork communications</td><td>Provider region and China</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Production and finishing partners</td><td>Print, die cut, laminate and pack a confirmed order</td><td>Order specification and artwork</td><td>China</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Freight forwarder and carrier</td><td>Transport, customs handover and delivery updates</td><td>Contact, address, parcel and invoice data</td><td>Origin, transit and destination</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Customs broker</td><td>Clearance administration</td><td>Commercial invoice, origin, value and consignee data</td><td>Destination country</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Accountant</td><td>Invoicing, tax and audit support</td><td>Invoice, payment and business identifier data</td><td>China or provider location</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>We do not sell personal data; an adviser, insurer or authority may receive limited data where the law requires it.</p>

      <h2>7. International transfers</h2>
      <p>
        Our team and production partners are in China, so data must be processed there to quote, print and ship. Where
        the GDPR or UK GDPR applies, we use Standard Contractual Clauses and, for the UK, the International Data
        Transfer Addendum, supported by a transfer risk assessment and access controls. The transfer is necessary to
        take pre-contract steps at your request and to perform a confirmed order; without it we could not quote or
        produce the work.
      </p>

      <h2>8. How long we keep data</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Retention</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Enquiries without an order</td><td>24 months</td><td>Follow-up and quotation history</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Orders and invoices</td><td>For the period required by applicable accounting and tax law</td><td>Record-keeping and audit</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Artwork and proofs</td><td>Production plus 24 months, unless you request earlier deletion</td><td>Reorder support without repeated setup</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Server and security logs</td><td>30 days</td><td>Abuse and incident investigation</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Consent records</td><td>24 months after the permission ends</td><td>To show the scope and duration of consent</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>At the end of a period we delete or anonymise data unless a legal hold, dispute or mandatory rule requires a longer record.</p>

      <h2>9. Your privacy rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to local law, you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability or objection,
        withdraw consent and complain to a supervisory authority. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Privacy request`}>{site.email}</a> with enough information to identify
        the records. We respond within 30 days and will explain any lawful extension.
      </p>

      <h2>10. UK and California rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the UK GDPR you may complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener">UK
        Information Commissioner's Office</a>; we would prefer the chance to resolve the issue first. Where the CPRA
        applies, you may request to know, delete or correct personal information without discriminatory treatment. We
        do not sell personal information, do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising and do not
        intentionally collect sensitive personal information for a business purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Security and breach notification</h2>
      <p>
        Access is limited to the team and processors who need it, through access-controlled email and hosting
        accounts, and we do not collect card details through the site. No system is perfectly secure. If a breach
        creates a risk to your rights, we will investigate, contain it and notify affected people and the competent
        authority where required. Where the GDPR applies, we aim to notify the authority without undue delay and
        within 72 hours of becoming aware of a notifiable breach.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Children and automated decisions</h2>
      <p>
        This business service is not directed at children under 16, and we do not knowingly collect their data. We do
        not make automated decisions with legal or similarly significant effects and do not create behavioural or
        advertising profiles; a person reviews each quotation.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>
        Only strictly necessary Cloudflare security cookies may be set. There are no analytics, advertising or
        personalisation cookies, and our site code does not write to localStorage or sessionStorage. See the
        <a href="/cookies/">cookies page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If a practice, processor category or retention period changes, we update this page before the change goes live
        and revise the review date. A material change affecting an existing order will be communicated where the law
        requires it.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Contact and complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}?subject=Privacy`}>{site.email}</a> with the subject “Privacy” for any
        access, correction, deletion, objection or policy question. You may also complain to your local data
        protection authority.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Related policies: <a href="/cookies/">Cookies</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms</a> ·
        <a href="/refund-policy/">Returns</a> · <a href="/shipping-delivery/">Shipping</a> ·
        <a href="/declarations/">Declarations</a> · <a href="/editorial-standards/">Editorial standards</a> ·
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a> · <a href="/corrections/">Corrections</a> ·
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/accessibility/">Accessibility</a> ·
        <a href="/contact/">Contact</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
